# Build context: the Dockerfiles only copy pyproject.toml, uv.lock and src/.
# Everything else is left out, so neither data (bind-mounted at run time),
# models (pulled from the registry, or mounted), secrets (.env, user accounts)
# nor local state ever ends up in an image or slows the build down.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src/

# Python caches inside src/
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
